1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,222
What needs attention in your VMware environment?

2
00:00:03,222 --> 00:00:12,888
VMware Skills connects an AI assistant to focused skills and MCP tools, helping engineers investigate infrastructure and plan their next steps.

3
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:19,638
The family covers vSphere, networking, storage, observability and more.

4
00:00:19,638 --> 00:00:21,818
Pilot coordinates workflows.

5
00:00:21,818 --> 00:00:25,727
Domain servers connect to their management systems.

6
00:00:25,727 --> 00:00:30,464
Policy provides shared checks, sanitization and audit logging.

7
00:00:30,464 --> 00:00:33,020
Start with the read-only Monitor.

8
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:38,173
Here is a historical screenshot from an actual session.

9
00:00:38,173 --> 00:00:43,681
The inventory view returned one vCenter, two standalone hosts, and thirteen VMs.

10
00:00:43,681 --> 00:00:48,033
The notes column containing environment identifiers is omitted.

11
00:00:48,033 --> 00:00:52,793
These are recorded results, not a fresh inventory of the environment.

12
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:59,180
The health screenshot records connected hosts and critical alarms in the same view.

13
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:01,820
That does not establish a current incident.

14
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:08,840
Check when the observation was captured and whether the alarms still apply before deciding what to investigate next.

15
00:01:10,267 --> 00:01:15,638
When changes are needed, use the relevant domain skill and a reviewed workflow.

16
00:01:15,638 --> 00:01:19,581
Existing VMware permissions and local policy still apply.

17
00:01:19,581 --> 00:01:23,252
Destructive tools use preview and confirmation gates.

18
00:01:23,252 --> 00:01:28,963
A confirmation flag is not independent human approval, and rollback is best effort.

19
00:01:30,367 --> 00:01:32,665
Finally, follow the audit trail.

20
00:01:32,665 --> 00:01:41,213
This is an assistant-prepared summary of exported records, showing time, skill, tool, MCP or CLI, status and duration.

21
00:01:41,213 --> 00:01:44,805
We omit the target column and show fourteen rows.

22
00:01:44,805 --> 00:01:50,839
Names reflect the captured version; use the original records to check completeness.

23
00:01:52,267 --> 00:01:58,493
VMware Skills is a community open-source project, not an official VMware or Broadcom product.

24
00:01:58,493 --> 00:02:04,452
Explore the demos, try a read-only task, and share what works or what needs improvement.

25
00:02:04,452 --> 00:02:09,139
If it helps your work, star the family portal to help others find it.
